<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-nŏcŭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>harmless</i>, <i>innocuous</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luporum genus innocuum homini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 34, 52, § 123</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imber leguminibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					18, 17, 44, § 152</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 800</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litus,</span>”
				<i>safe</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 230</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>unharmed</i>, <i>uninjured</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sedere carinae omnes innocuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 302</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fida per innocuas errent incendia turres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Cons. Mall. Theod. 330</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>inoffensive</i>,
				<i>innocent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viximus innocuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 373</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agere causas innocuas,</span>”
				<i>to defend the innocent</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 2, 273</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innocuum perforat ense latus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 3, 9, 26</span></i>
			. — Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innŏcŭē</span></b> . </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Harmlessly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sagittas tanta arte direxit, ut omnes per
					intervalla digitorum innocue evaderent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 19</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Innocently</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 1, 640</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
